menu "Toothbrush timer"

    config TOOTHBRUSH_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "LCD pixel clock (MHz)"
        range 8 24
        default 18
        help
            Refresh rate is pclk / (548 * 508): 16 MHz ~57 Hz, 18 MHz ~65 Hz.
            Below ~12 MHz colored backgrounds visibly pulse in intensity. With bounce buffers the
            PSRAM frame buffer keeps up at higher clocks; lower this if the picture shifts or tears.

    config TOOTHBRUSH_LCD_BOUNCE_LINES
        int "LCD bounce buffer height (lines)"
        range 4 40
        default 10
        help
            Height of each of the two internal-RAM bounce buffers (480 pixels per line, 2 bytes per
            pixel). Must divide 480. Larger buffers tolerate longer PSRAM stalls but use more RAM.

endmenu
